issues.description:
**Description:**

In production, the reverse proxy injects a `personaUserName` HTTP header on every request. `Session/Login` is `[AllowAnonymous]` and reads this header unconditionally. When a user logs out, the app clears its cookies and session, but the proxy continues injecting the header. Something on the disclaimer page (`Home/Index`) triggers a navigation to `Session/Login`, which re-authenticates the user immediately, causing the "blink and back to the list" behavior.

**Root cause files:**

* [Source/OneNListApp.Web/Controllers/SessionController.cs](vscode-webview://0nfnc11nghrep6s3jh3und5rh4tbkta95dj880h1qbj3egeupg18/Source/OneNListApp.Web/Controllers/SessionController.cs) — `Logout()` line 116, `Login()` line 50
* [Source/OneNListApp.Web/Views/Home/Index.cshtml](vscode-webview://0nfnc11nghrep6s3jh3und5rh4tbkta95dj880h1qbj3egeupg18/Source/OneNListApp.Web/Views/Home/Index.cshtml) — "I Agree" link

**Changes required:**

**1. `Logout()` — set an explicit logout flag (redirect destination unchanged — stays `Home/Index`):**

`public async Task<IActionResult> Logout()
{
    await HttpContext.SignOutAsync(IdentityConstants.ApplicationScheme);
    SessionManager.ClearSession();
    SessionManager.RemoveCookie();
    TempData.Remove("personaUserName");

    // Set AFTER ClearSession — session ID persists even after values are cleared
    HttpContext.Session.SetString("ExplicitlyLoggedOut", "true");

    return RedirectToAction("Index", "Home"); // User returned to disclaimer page
}
`

**2. `Login()` — guard against automatic re-authentication; allow intentional login via `?explicit=1`:**

`[AllowAnonymous]
public async Task<IActionResult> Login()
{
    bool isExplicitLogin = Request.Query["explicit"] == "1";

    if (HttpContext.Session.GetString("ExplicitlyLoggedOut") == "true")
    {
        if (!isExplicitLogin)
            return RedirectToAction("Index", "Home"); // Break the auto-loop

        // User deliberately clicked I Agree — clear flag and proceed
        HttpContext.Session.Remove("ExplicitlyLoggedOut");
    }

    string personaUsername = HttpContext.Request.Headers["personaUserName"];
    // ... rest unchanged
`

**3. Update the "I Agree" link in the disclaimer to include `?explicit=1`:**

[Source/OneNListApp.Web/Views/Home/Index.cshtml](vscode-webview://0nfnc11nghrep6s3jh3und5rh4tbkta95dj880h1qbj3egeupg18/Source/OneNListApp.Web/Views/Home/Index.cshtml) line 43 — change:

`<a DisableOnCLick class="btn btn-lg btn-primary" 
   href="@Url.Content("~/Session/Login")?@Html.CopySrcQueryString()">I Agree</a>
`

to:

`<a DisableOnCLick class="btn btn-lg btn-primary" 
   href="@Url.Content("~/Session/Login")?explicit=1&@Html.CopySrcQueryString()">I Agree</a>
`

**Acceptance Criteria:**

*  Clicking Logout returns the user to the disclaimer page (`Home/Index`), not the list
  * [ ]  After landing on the disclaimer page, the user is NOT automatically re-authenticated (no blink/redirect back to the list)
  * [ ]  Clicking "I Agree" on the disclaimer after logout successfully logs the user back in and proceeds to the list normally
  * [ ]  `SessionExpiredLogout` is unaffected — it does not set the flag (expired sessions re-authenticate on next visit)
  * [ ]  Users without the `ExplicitlyLoggedOut` flag (first visit, new browser session) log in normally — no behavior change

**Unit Test Requirements:**

Add to [Source/OneNListApp.Tests/Web/SessionControllerLoginTests.cs](vscode-webview://0nfnc11nghrep6s3jh3und5rh4tbkta95dj880h1qbj3egeupg18/Source/OneNListApp.Tests/Web/SessionControllerLoginTests.cs):

* `Logout_SetsExplicitlyLoggedOutSessionFlag` — after calling `Logout()`, assert session contains `"ExplicitlyLoggedOut" = "true"`
* `Logout_RedirectsToHomeIndex` — assert redirect target is `Index`/`Home`
* `Login_WhenFlagSetAndNoExplicitParam_RedirectsToHomeIndex_WithoutSigningIn` — mock session with flag set, call `Login()` without `?explicit=1`, assert redirect to `Home/Index` and `SignInAsync` NOT called
* `Login_WhenFlagSetAndExplicitParam_ClearsFlagAndProceeds` — mock session with flag set, call `Login()` with `?explicit=1`, assert flag removed from session and `SignInAsync` IS called
* `Login_WhenNoFlag_ProcessesNormally` — confirm existing behavior unchanged when flag absent

Add E2E test in [Source/OneNListApp.E2E/](vscode-webview://0nfnc11nghrep6s3jh3und5rh4tbkta95dj880h1qbj3egeupg18/Source/OneNListApp.E2E/):

* `Logout_LandsOnDisclaimerPage_NotList` — click logout, assert URL is `Home/Index` and list table is not present
* `Logout_ThenClickIAgree_LogsBackInSuccessfully` — after logout, click I Agree, assert redirect to list completes
